def smallest_change(arr):
    """
    Given an array arr of integers, find the minimum number of elements that
    need to be changed to make the array palindromic. A palindromic array is an array that
    reads the same backwards and forwards. In one change, you can change one element to any other element.

    The minimum number of changes is equal to the number of pairs of elements at symmetric positions
    from the start and end of the array that differ, counting each such pair as exactly one change 
    (changing one element of the pair to match the other).

    For example:
    smallest_change([1,2,3,5,4,7,9,6]) == 4
    smallest_change([1, 2, 3, 4, 3, 2, 2]) == 1
    smallest_change([1, 2, 3, 2, 1]) == 0
    """
    n = len(arr)
